@namespace DotNetCloud.Modules.Chat.UI

@*
    Help content for the Chat module.
*@

<div class="help-content">
    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Overview</h2>
        <p>DotNetCloud Chat is a real-time messaging platform supporting channels, direct messages, file sharing, and audio/video calls. Stay connected with your team in organized conversation spaces.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Channels</h2>
        <p><strong>Public channels</strong> are visible to all users and are great for team-wide discussions. <strong>Private channels</strong> are invite-only for specific groups.</p>
        <p><strong>Creating a channel:</strong> Click the <strong>+</strong> button in the Chat sidebar, enter a name, choose a type (<strong>Public</strong> or <strong>Private</strong>), and click <strong>Create</strong>.</p>
        <p><strong>Channel actions:</strong> From the channel header you can <strong>Pin</strong> a channel to the top of the sidebar (drag pinned channels to reorder them), <strong>Mute</strong> its notifications, <strong>Invite</strong> a user, <strong>Add People</strong>, <strong>Edit</strong> its name and topic, <strong>Archive</strong>, or <strong>Leave</strong> it. Owners and admins can manage members from the member list. Use the search box in the sidebar to find channels.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Direct Messages</h2>
        <p>Start a direct message with <strong>New DM</strong>. Direct messages are private between participants. You can block a user — a blocked user cannot send you messages or call you.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Messaging</h2>
        <p>Type your message in the input bar and press <kbd>Enter</kbd> to send, or <kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>Enter</kbd> for a new line. Use the formatting toolbar for bold, italic, code blocks, and quotes, the emoji picker, and the <strong>@@</strong> symbol to mention someone with autocomplete.</p>
        <p><strong>Attachments:</strong> Attach files or paste an image from your clipboard. Hover over a message to <strong>Reply</strong>, <strong>Edit</strong>, <strong>Delete</strong>, or add a reaction.</p>
        <p><strong>Search:</strong> Use the search icon in the channel header to find messages within the current channel.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Audio &amp; Video Calls</h2>
        <p>Start an audio or video call from a channel or direct message with the <strong>Call</strong> buttons in the header. In a call you can mute, turn your camera on or off, share your screen, and invite more people. If a call is already active, use <strong>Join Call</strong>. The <strong>Calls</strong> button shows call history with a call-back option.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Announcements &amp; Notifications</h2>
        <p>Administrators can post announcements that appear as a banner at the top of the chat. Open your notification preferences to enable push notifications and manage per-channel mute settings.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Tips &amp; Tricks</h2>
        <ul class="help-tips">
            <li>Use channels for topic-specific discussions and DMs for private conversations.</li>
            <li>Pin frequently used channels to the top of the sidebar for quick access.</li>
            <li>Mute noisy channels and use search to find messages within a channel.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</div>
